From 77c823708facca63364475b084dc316f2ddc7337 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gnanaprakash Elumalai <gelumala@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 15:25:50 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] prplMesh: fix static analysis safety findings

Problem:
- Several runtime paths lacked pointer and payload validation.
- Arithmetic and TLVF length handling could overflow or underflow.
- Generated variable-length allocation code modified state before
  validation and used unsafe overlapping copies.
- Some generated fields had incorrect or unsafe initialization.
- Enum string fallback storage was not thread-safe.

RCA:
- Input validation and allocation failure handling were incomplete.
- TLVF generator templates did not consistently validate lengths before
  modifying buffers and object state.
- Optional fields were initialized before being allocated.
- Generated defaults and protocol identifiers were incorrect in several
  definitions.

Fix:
- Add null, HAL-result, divisor, and event-payload validation.
- Reset failed ARP registration state.
- Add serialized-length overflow and TLV-length underflow checks.
- Reserve buffer capacity before updating indexes, counters, and pointers.
- Replace overlapping std::copy_n operations with checked std::memmove.
- Initialize optional structures only after successful allocation.
- Correct QoS element ID and optional-field defaults.
- Make enum fallback strings thread-local.
- Update TLVF generators and YAML definitions so regeneration preserves
  the fixes.

Signed-off-by: Gnanaprakash Elumalai <gelumala@qti.qualcomm.com>
